From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:38:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hegel_draw_url_alloc: a URL draw that cannot be truncated

hegel_draw_url writes into the caller's buffer and cuts the URL at
capacity - 1 bytes.  URLs have no length bound (631 characters seen in
2000 draws, TODO.md), and a cut URL is not a valid one, so a harness with
a short buffer tests malformed input without knowing.

hegel_draw_url_alloc (tc) makes the same engine draw (HEGEL_OP_DRAW_URL,
same choices) and returns the whole string in a hegel_alloc block: owned
by the case, freed on every exit path, like hegel_draw_grammar's result.
hegel_draw_url is unchanged.

test_value_draws_net draws one and checks its shape; CLAUDE.md, the C
skill reference and TODO.md name it.

Not built or run: written in a sandbox that could not compile the
repository.  Run make selftest-test before keeping it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
